  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You call forth a Fey spirit. It appears in an unoccupied space you can see within range and uses the Fey Spirit stat block. When you cast the spell, choose a mood: Fuming, Mirthful, or Tricksy. The creature looks like a Fey creature of your choice marked by that mood, which determines some details of its stat block. It disappears when it drops to 0 Hit Points or when the spell ends.</p><p>The creature is an ally to you and your allies. In combat, it shares your Initiative count but takes its turn immediately after yours. It obeys your verbal commands (no action required by you); if you give none, it takes the Dodge action and uses its movement to avoid danger.</p><p><strong>Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.</strong> Use the spell slot’s level for the spell’s level in the stat block.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-9LRcAF5JvFQo0mHA\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Summon asks for the mood. The spirit’s AC, Hit Points and Fey Blade damage include the spell’s level, and its saving throw DC is your spell save DC.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
